    <GaugingStation location="Ormiston Mill" name="Teviot" number="21008">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station d/s of Hawick on the River Teviot.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Natural channel control. Rock and gravel section at gauge with d/s gravel riffle giving low flow control. Rating subject to appreciable weed growth. Multiple peak flow ratings derived from current meter gaugings up to 3.4m (about 1.1 QMED), simple extrapolation beyond. Bypassing occurs on the rb (golf course side) at levels above 2.2m, and bypasses behind the cableway.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity area station; about 45m wide section.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in August 2021 (WINFAP Files v10) and September 2022 (WINFAP Files v11).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Catchment contains two small storages (Alemoor Loch, Akermoor Loch) but runoff is sensibly natural.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Mostly lowland catchment with upland headwaters. Mainly Silurian shale and ORS; 70% overlain by superficial deposits. Land use chiefly moorland and hill grazing with some arable farming towards the confluence with the Tweed; some forested areas in the uplands. No significant catchment changes known. Notable floodplains.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged to QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Although higher ranking events are up to 2m above bankfull (estimated 3m), pictures show that floodplain flow is not extensive. Given this and gaugings up to bank full level, there is reasonable confidence in the estimates of the larger floods, allowing a tentative pooling classification." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
